  "id": "BIT-postgresql-2026-120149",
  "summary": "PostgreSQL FDW batch-insert mismatch executes arbitrary code",
  "details": "Heap-based buffer overflow in PostgreSQL foreign batch inserts allows a foreign server to execute arbitrary code, via reporting that it inserted more rows than the server supplied.  postgres_fdw can legitimately encounter this when a rule on the remote table expands an INSERT into additional rows.  Versions before PostgreSQL 18.7, 17.12, 16.16, 15.20, and 14.25 are affected.",
